From dad5b5b9c0ac12b7a3bdf498c9218613e0a760e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JeyKul <minkajey@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:40:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] drm: exynos2200: DSIM takeover and panel backlight

Exynos 2200 DSIM driver that takes over the DSI link the bootloader
left running (DECON0, command mode, DSC). With the bootloader's DSIM
state no DCS command reaches the panel; after Samsung's re-init
sequence (DECON's TE trigger paused, panel untouched) they do. The
bootloader's TE protect/timeout window is kept.

The Galaxy S22 Ultra panel (S6E3HAE) brightness is exposed as a
backlight (DCS 51h behind the level 1/2 keys, then a gamma update),
normal range only. A debugfs file sends raw DCS commands.

The register layer in cal/ is Samsung's GPL DSIM cal from the s5e9925
kernel (dsim_reg.c, regs-dsim.h, dsim_cal.h, cal_config.h,
exynos_panel.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
